# --workers 1 is REQUIRED, not a performance choice.
#
# Three pieces of state live in the API process's memory and are not shared
# between workers:
#
#   app/websocket/manager.py         connected admin sockets
#   app/websocket/session_manager.py connected student sockets, per session
#   app/core/step_up.py              failed password-confirmation counters
#
# Gunicorn's worker count defaults to the WEB_CONCURRENCY environment
# variable (gunicorn/config.py), which a host may set on its own. With more
# than one worker, a monitoring event created on worker A would only reach
# the admins connected to worker A, an invigilator's pause would only reach
# a student attached to the same worker, and the step-up lockout would allow
# five attempts PER worker. Each of those fails silently and intermittently
# -- the features appear to work, then do not.
#
# Pinning this makes the deployment match what the code assumes. Sharing
# that state (a database table or a pub/sub channel) is what would be needed
# before scaling past one worker.
web: gunicorn app.main:app --worker-class uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker --workers 1 --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT
